  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35733946",
      "title": "More loader() Data Usage",
      "sourceHash": "a1a8c586bf2a7bf4f79f8a76974244de5eacd718c31849b8bf80687b87889627",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.58,
          "end": 4.53,
          "en": "Now before we dive deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.53,
          "end": 6.84,
          "en": "into this entire loader thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.84,
          "end": 9.63,
          "en": "and also talk about error handling and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.63,
          "end": 13.86,
          "en": "let's see where else we could use this useLoaderData hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.86,
          "end": 15.6,
          "en": "We can use it in this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.6,
          "end": 19.59,
          "en": "which is rendered by the route on which we added the loader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.59,
          "end": 21.123,
          "en": "but where else can we use it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.32,
          "end": 24.33,
          "en": "Well, we could also use it directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.33,
          "end": 26.253,
          "en": "inside the EventsList component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.09,
          "end": 29.4,
          "en": "So instead of using it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.4,
          "end": 31.26,
          "en": "and instead of importing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.26,
          "end": 34.08,
          "en": "we could go to this EventsList component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.08,
          "end": 36.18,
          "en": "and use this hook there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.18,
          "end": 39.28,
          "en": "Here we can also import useLoaderData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.29,
          "end": 42.183,
          "en": "from react-router-dom,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.26,
          "end": 45.18,
          "en": "and then call this in this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.18,
          "end": 47.67,
          "en": "even though it's not a page component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.67,
          "end": 49.56,
          "en": "But there technically is no difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.56,
          "end": 52.71,
          "en": "between page components and other components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.71,
          "end": 55.17,
          "en": "so therefore we can use it here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.17,
          "end": 56.46,
          "en": "And if we do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 56.46,
          "end": 58.29,
          "en": "you will see that this events object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 58.29,
          "end": 60.33,
          "en": "which we're getting here will be available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 60.33,
          "end": 62.19,
          "en": "and everything will work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 62.19,
          "end": 65.55,
          "en": "I just need to make sure that I'm no longer waiting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 65.55,
          "end": 69.27,
          "en": "for events props here, which I try to destructure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 69.27,
          "end": 71.01,
          "en": "But if I remove those props here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 71.01,
          "end": 72.33,
          "en": "you will see everything works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 72.33,
          "end": 75.78,
          "en": "and I am fetching and rendering those events successfully.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 75.78,
          "end": 76.893,
          "en": "So that works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 78.51,
          "end": 82.17,
          "en": "Now, one place where we can't get those events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 82.17,
          "end": 84.51,
          "en": "is in a higher level route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 84.51,
          "end": 87.48,
          "en": "So for example, if you would go to the RootLayout here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 87.48,
          "end": 89.913,
          "en": "which is part of my root route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 90.78,
          "end": 95.78,
          "en": "If I go to this RootLayout and I useLoaderData here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 96.21000000000001,
          "end": 99.09,
          "en": "by first of all importing useLoaderData,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.2,
          "end": 102.39,
          "en": "and then calling that hook here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 102.39,
          "end": 105.57,
          "en": "you will see that if I try to get my events here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 105.57,
          "end": 108.47999999999999,
          "en": "and I console log my events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.47999999999999,
          "end": 111.18,
          "en": "this will not work as expected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.18,
          "end": 113.793,
          "en": "Instead, it logs undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 115.14,
          "end": 118.35,
          "en": "The reason for that is that I'm trying to get data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.35,
          "end": 123.03,
          "en": "from a route that's actually defined on a lower level.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.03,
          "end": 127.08,
          "en": "I'm trying to get data that's loaded from this route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.08,
          "end": 131.13,
          "en": "in this root route, which is on a much higher level.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.13,
          "end": 133.8,
          "en": "After all, this is a deeply nested route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.8,
          "end": 135.84,
          "en": "and that's not possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.84,
          "end": 138.42000000000002,
          "en": "Instead, you can access loaded data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.42000000000002,
          "end": 139.72,
          "en": "with help of useLoaderData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 140.57999999999998,
          "end": 144.48,
          "en": "in any component on the same level or lower level",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.48,
          "end": 147.3,
          "en": "than the component where you added the loader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.3,
          "end": 150.09,
          "en": "so the route on which you added the loader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 150.09,
          "end": 151.68,
          "en": "So that is simply how that works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 151.68,
          "end": 154.05,
          "en": "and what you should keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 154.05,
          "end": 157.5,
          "en": "With that, I will actually change my code again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 157.5,
          "end": 160.77,
          "en": "and useLoaderData in the Events page component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 160.77,
          "end": 163.26,
          "en": "and bring back that events property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 163.26,
          "end": 166.49,
          "en": "on which I pass my events queue EventsList,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 167.37,
          "end": 170.49,
          "en": "and I will get rid of my loader data usage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 170.49,
          "end": 171.99,
          "en": "here in EventsList,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 171.99,
          "end": 175.14,
          "en": "and instead bring back this object destructure here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 175.14,
          "end": 180.03,
          "en": "in my parameter list to extract the events from my props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 180.03,
          "end": 182.31,
          "en": "With that, it again, all works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 182.31,
          "end": 184.44,
          "en": "but now with that original approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 184.44,
          "end": 187.26,
          "en": "where I useLoaderData in my page component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 187.26,
          "end": 188.76,
          "en": "Ultimately, it's up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 188.76,
          "end": 190.38,
          "en": "You just have to be careful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 190.38,
          "end": 193.427,
          "en": "that you're not accidentally using useLoaderData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 193.427,
          "end": 195.873,
          "en": "on a higher level than you're fetching the data.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}